        "hypotheses": "Let S be any finite set of primes and P its product, with P=1 if S is empty. Set M=P. Choose arbitrarily large positive integers L≡1 mod P and t_i=iP/L for i=1,2,3,4. Take L sufficiently large that all t_i lie in an interval (0,ε) on which F is strictly increasing and 0<F(t)<1.",
